; Policy for a plant run: one capability, and it is the machine.
;
; No local_shell, no simulator, no memory. The agent's entire reach is the
; channel table passed on the command line — this file says "may write", the
; table says "what, and between which numbers". A model denied a setpoint has
; nothing else to reach for, which is the same property examples/machine-policy.spg
; buys for pause/resume.
;
; Granting `device` grants the right to move a physical thing, and it is
; deliberately separate from machine_process: an operator who wanted an agent
; that may pause a runaway process must not silently also get one that may
; drive a heater.
(policy
 (network_default deny)
 (budgets
  (inference_steps 8)
  (tokens 256)
  (shell_actions 0)
  (sim_actions 0)
  (memory_actions 0)
  (wall_ms 10000)
  ; device_write consumes machine_actions — it shares the budget with
  ; pause/resume while keeping its own capability.
  (machine_actions 4))
 (capability
  ((name device) (kind device) (enabled true) (budget 4))))